# The FastAPI backend deploys WITH the frontend: api/index.py serves it as a
# Python function on the same origin (see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md). So backend/apps/
# must ship, and is no longer listed below; its tests, scripts and datasets
# still stay out.
#
# Two more directories the frontend needs are deliberately not ignored, because
# excluding them breaks the build or the running app rather than shrinking it:
#
#   colab/          — app/api/training/[task]/route.ts reads the notebooks from
#                     it at runtime. Next traces the directory, but tracing only
#                     sees files that were uploaded; ignoring it turns every
#                     notebook download into a 503 nothing warns about.
#   backend/models/ — lib/experiments.ts imports six model/history JSON files
#                     from it at build time. Ignoring it fails the build with
#                     "module not found" (1 MB, so the cost is nothing).
#
# backend/ is therefore excluded child by child rather than wholesale: with
# gitignore semantics a file cannot be re-included once its parent directory is
# excluded, so "backend/" plus a negation would not work.
backend/apps/api/tests/
backend/datasets/
backend/docs/
backend/scripts/
backend/storage/
backend/tasks/
backend/tests/
backend/Dockerfile
backend/docker-compose.yml
backend/*.md
output/
tmp/
docs/
prisma/
scripts/
SUMMARY.md
SUMMARY.pdf
tasks/
.pytest_cache/
node_modules
.next
*.tsbuildinfo

# Defence in depth. Vercel already skips these because .gitignore does, but a
# real .env reaching a third party should not depend on a second file's rules.
.env
.env.*
!.env*.example
.venv/
backend/.venv/
